---
import { site } from "../config";

interface Props {
  /**
   * "bar" is the horizontal row in the header, which is what Hugo renders.
   * "panel" is the stacked list inside the drop-down, added on 2026-09-09 for narrow
   * viewports; it has no counterpart in Hugo. Both variants live here so that the
   * aria-current rules below - which encode Hugo's semantics - have exactly one home.
   */
  variant?: "bar" | "panel";
}

const { variant = "bar" } = Astro.props;

const path = Astro.url.pathname;

// Hugo marks the entry that is the current page with IsMenuCurrent (`aria-current="page"`)
// and the entry whose section contains the current page with HasMenuCurrent
// (`aria-current="true"`). Checked against the Hugo build for every route: only
// /posts/<slug>/ ever produced an ancestor match, and taxonomy term pages (/tags/hugo/,
// /categories/blog/) marked nothing at all.
//
// Changed 2026-09-19 evening, asked for by the owner: the menu is to show which section the
// reader is in, so every entry but Home is the ancestor of the pages under its address -
// Posts of /posts/2026/ and of an article, Tags of /tags/hugo/, Categories of
// /categories/blog/. That goes beyond Hugo's HasMenuCurrent, which ignores taxonomy terms.
// Home matches only the home page itself.
function ariaCurrent(url: string): "page" | "true" | undefined {
  if (path === url) return "page";
  if (url !== "/" && path.startsWith(url)) return "true";
  return undefined;
}

// The Hugo partial also merges an "active font-bold" / "ancestor font-semibold" class into
// the same link, which produces a SECOND class attribute next to the literal one:
//   <a class="px-2 py-1 ..." aria-current="page" class="active font-bold" href="/">
// Browsers keep the first class attribute and drop the second, and neither `.active` nor
// `.ancestor` is styled anywhere in the theme - so on the live Hugo site the current menu
// item is NOT bold, and until 2026-09-19 this port left the classes out to render the same.
//
// Changed 2026-09-19 evening, asked for by the owner: the classes are merged into the one
// class attribute now, through class:list, so the current page's entry is bold and its
// section's entry semibold - what the theme's author wrote and never saw. `active` and
// `ancestor` stay as hooks. The weight alone turned out too subtle - the owner did not
// notice it - so both states also take the colours of the year switcher's highlighted
// button (YearSwitcher.astro), the site's existing "you are here" look: blue-50 with
// blue-700 text, slate-700 with blue-300 in dark mode. The link's own hover classes still
// win on hover. See README, "The active menu item is highlighted", and MIGRATION-PLAN.md
// section 9.
const currentClasses = (current: "page" | "true" | undefined) => [
  current === "page" && "active font-bold",
  current === "true" && "ancestor font-semibold",
  current && "bg-blue-50 text-blue-700 dark:bg-slate-700 dark:text-blue-300",
];

// Two changes to the Hugo class list in the "bar" variant, both inert at 768px and up, which
// is where the parity screenshots are taken:
//
// 1. `hidden sm:flex` on the nav, so the bar disappears below 640px and the hamburger in
//    Header.astro takes over.
// 2. The size bumps moved from `sm:` to `md:` - `md:space-x-6` on the list, `md:text-lg` on
//    the items, `md:px-3 md:py-2` on the links. Hugo grows the menu at 640px, but between
//    640px and 767px the grown row plus the title plus the theme toggle no longer fit: at
//    700px the row reached 680px against 661px of usable width, and because the header is
//    `fixed` the excess could not even be scrolled to - the theme toggle was simply cut off.
//    Keeping the compact sizes until 768px makes the row fit with room to spare, and at 768px
//    and up it is exactly what Hugo renders, `md:space-x-6` included. The owner chose to keep
//    the hamburger threshold at 640px, so this is what closes that band instead.
//
// Changed again on 2026-09-22, because the band moved rather than closed. Two things grew since
// that note was written: Video made a sixth menu item, and the logo is now painted at every width
// instead of only below 640px. Measured in a headless browser on the built page, row width
// against usable width: at a 656px viewport the row wanted 663px against 608px, and at 806px -
// just above the old md: threshold, where the bumps make everything bigger - it wanted 819px
// against 758px. Both spill to the right, and the header is `fixed`, so the end of the row and
// the theme toggle with it simply cannot be reached.
//
// Three changes, all of them inert at 1024px and up, where the row is again exactly what Hugo
// renders:
//
// 1. The size bumps moved from `md:` to `lg:`. The compact row now holds from 640px to 1024px,
//    which is the whole band where six items, the title, the logo and the switch have to share a
//    line.
// 2. `space-x-2` became `space-x-1` below that threshold: five gaps, 4px each.
// 3. The links are `px-1.5` instead of `px-2` below it: six links, 4px each.
//
// Header.astro trims the wrapper's side padding over the same band for the same reason. Together
// they take about 68px out of a row that was 55px too wide at its worst, and every width from
// 640px to 1600px was re-measured afterwards.
const isPanel = variant === "panel";
---

{
  isPanel ? (
    <nav class="w-full" aria-label="Site">
      <ul class="flex list-none flex-col">
        {site.menu.map((item) => (
          <li
            class:list={[
              "text-base text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-200",
              // members-only on every item but Home, added the evening of 2026-09-25: a guest's
              // header shows Home, the theme switch and the sign-in icon (the owner's list), and
              // custom.css hides the class until the gate in Base.astro marks the document
              // kb-member (AUTH.md section 10). The bar variant below does the same.
              item.url !== "/" && "members-only",
            ]}
          >
            <a
              class:list={[
                "block rounded px-2 py-3 transition-colors hover:bg-gray-100 hover:text-gray-900 dark:hover:bg-slate-800 dark:hover:text-white",
                ...currentClasses(ariaCurrent(item.url)),
              ]}
              aria-current={ariaCurrent(item.url)}
              href={item.url}
            >
              {item.name}
            </a>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </nav>
  ) : (
    <nav class="hidden w-full justify-end whitespace-nowrap sm:flex">
      {/* Changed 2026-09-22, the reviewer's remark that the items stand too far apart and the
        owner's instruction to halve it: from 1024px the gap was Hugo's space-x-6 (24px) and is
        space-x-3 (12px) now, and the links below lost lg:px-3 (12px a side) for the px-1.5 (6px)
        they already carry under that width. Five gaps and six links, so the row is about 132px
        narrower at desktop widths. That is a visible departure from Hugo, which is why it is in
        MIGRATION-PLAN.md section 9.

        The band from 640px to 1024px is deliberately left as it was, space-x-1 and px-1.5: those
        values are not a choice but the result of fitting six items, the title, the logo and the
        theme switch into one row, and halving 4px gives words that touch.

        Worth recording, because the history looks odd otherwise: the reviewer made the same
        change on main the same evening (commit 1bf0269, "Menu spacing"), lg:space-x-6 to
        lg:space-x-3, the identical value arrived at independently. Merging main into this branch
        conflicted on this block alone - the class itself merged cleanly because both sides had
        written the same thing - and the resolution kept this version, which is hers plus the
        padding on the links and this note. Nothing of hers was dropped. */}
      <ul class="flex list-none flex-row items-center space-x-1 py-2 lg:space-x-3">
        {site.menu.map((item) => (
          <li
            class:list={[
              "text-base text-gray-600 hover:text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-200 dark:hover:text-white lg:text-lg",
              // Same as the panel variant above (2026-09-25 evening, the guest gate).
              item.url !== "/" && "members-only",
            ]}
          >
            <a
              class:list={[
                // lg:px-3 dropped 2026-09-22 with the gap above: half of it is the px-1.5 this
                // line already sets, so the padding is now one value at every width. lg:py-2
                // stays - the reviewer measured the horizontal distance, and the height of the
                // bar is what decides where the carousel meets the header.
                "rounded px-1.5 py-1 transition-colors hover:bg-gray-100 dark:hover:bg-slate-800 lg:py-2",
                ...currentClasses(ariaCurrent(item.url)),
              ]}
              aria-current={ariaCurrent(item.url)}
              href={item.url}
            >
              {item.name}
            </a>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </nav>
  )
}
